 "verdicts": {
  "Cognition found that relying on Sonnet 4.5's self-written notes without its own compaction and summarization systems caused performance degradation and knowledge gaps, because the notes sometimes paraphrased the task and omitted details.": 1,
  "With Claude Sonnet 4.5, Cognition observed 'context anxiety': the model took shortcuts or left tasks incomplete when it believed it neared its context limit, even with room left; Cognition countered with reminders at both the start and end of prompts and by enabling the 1M token beta while capping usage at 200k.": 1
 }
